WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.967
- So at 30, I started Wine
Library TV, YouTube blows up.

00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:06.845
At 31 I'm on 
Conan O'Brien, Ellen,

00:00:06.845 --> 00:00:08.164
there's articles being 
written about me,

00:00:08.164 --> 00:00:09.516
now they're writing 
that the business grew

00:00:09.516 --> 00:00:12.054
from three to 
60 million dollars in sales,

00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:13.467
I'm becoming this guy.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:17.243
I got so many goddamn emails
from friends in high school,

00:00:17.243 --> 00:00:18.673
during that period 
when I was showing up

00:00:18.673 --> 00:00:20.878
in all these 
magazines and TV shows,

00:00:20.878 --> 00:00:23.226
and every single 
one of them, was like

00:00:23.226 --> 00:00:24.900
"Hey Gary, you remember
me from high school?

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.734
"Oh my God, you're so lucky."

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:30.334
I wrote back every single
one of them, and said,

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.893
"Let me just clarify one
thing, I'm not lucky,

00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:36.684
"I worked. I worked every goddamn
weekend and every holiday,

00:00:36.684 --> 00:00:38.212
"since I was 14 years old,

00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:40.800
"so you can keep that
luck shit in your pocket."

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.967
("Inertia" by Irregular Expression)

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:49.157
Every day, every day 
that I live my life,

00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:52.903
I get five to 27 
emails from people

00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:55.813
that are telling me
that they are quitting,

00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:57.632
or they should quit, or,

00:00:57.632 --> 00:01:00.677
or are really coming
to me as a last resort

00:01:00.677 --> 00:01:04.565
to convince them not to quit
I think a lot of times, or,

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.692
or maybe give them confirmation
that they should quit.

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:10.014
You know, "Hey Gary, this is Sally,

00:01:10.014 --> 00:01:12.206
"I've been doing my
blog now for nine months

00:01:12.206 --> 00:01:15.672
"and I'm not getting the
results that I like to see

00:01:15.672 --> 00:01:19.474
"or that I was promised"
or that, you innuendo.

00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:22.024
"Should I give up, like,
you know, should I,

00:01:22.024 --> 00:01:24.105
"is my content not good enough,

00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:26.248
"am I, is my voice 
not good enough?"

00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:28.616
And I think about it, every time,

00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:30.197
every time I see these emails,

00:01:30.197 --> 00:01:33.003
every time people ask me at
conferences I think about it,

00:01:33.003 --> 00:01:35.444
I think about how sad I am

00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:37.894
that I wasn't documenting my life,

00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:41.357
or putting out content, or
doing The #AskGaryVee Show,

00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:45.524
during those five and a half
years of Wine Library TV,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.947
especially those 18 months
when nobody was watching.

00:01:51.603 --> 00:01:53.366
You know the story 
that's never told,

00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:56.824
is the story that I was
building Wine Library

00:01:56.824 --> 00:01:59.700
to a huge company long
before Wine Library TV,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.669
and that the first month
that I did Wine Library TV,

00:02:03.669 --> 00:02:05.830
was the first time that Wine Library

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:10.467
had not grown 30% over
the prior year's revenue.

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:14.569
So not only did 
I have the patience

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:18.048
to let it play itself out and win,

00:02:18.048 --> 00:02:21.154
it was a scenario where 
I was actually losing money

00:02:21.154 --> 00:02:22.599
by being patient.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.496
Many of the people that are
going to watch this video

00:02:24.496 --> 00:02:26.581
are not achieving what they want,

00:02:26.581 --> 00:02:28.026
and are lacking the patience,

00:02:28.026 --> 00:02:30.265
and think everything happens overnight,

00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:33.531
and that is coming at the
cost of an unhappy life,

00:02:33.531 --> 00:02:36.513
or no loss financially, 
just loss in time.

00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:40.067
Just coming at the 
expense of Angry Birds,

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:44.441
or House of Cards marathons,
or the bowling team,

00:02:44.441 --> 00:02:46.888
or hanging out with
friends and having a beer,

00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:48.867
or reading a magazine,

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:53.434
or whatever the hell gets you
off and excited as a hobby.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.664
It's coming at that expense,

00:02:54.664 --> 00:02:56.915
it's not coming at the
expense of actual money,

00:02:56.915 --> 00:02:59.277
or something, or pain, 
or, you know,

00:02:59.277 --> 00:03:01.992
it's coming at the 
expense of a luxury.

00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:03.075
And so to me,

00:03:05.512 --> 00:03:08.149
the insanity, really, and
that's what I'm gonna,

00:03:08.149 --> 00:03:10.941
you know, the disproportional
misunderstanding

00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:13.881
that there's not a person
that you can name, not one,

00:03:13.881 --> 00:03:16.740
there is zero people that you can name,

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.274
that had it happen overnight.

00:03:18.274 --> 00:03:21.347
Even the nine year-old 
Stevie Wonder

00:03:21.347 --> 00:03:23.708
and six year-old 
Michael Jackson,

00:03:23.708 --> 00:03:26.897
there were years 
of work put in prior

00:03:26.897 --> 00:03:28.878
by their parents, by their uncles.

00:03:28.878 --> 00:03:31.741
Even with the greatest
talents, even with LeBron,

00:03:31.741 --> 00:03:33.638
he seemed like so young
when he hit the scene.

00:03:33.638 --> 00:03:34.926
Guess what, he wasn't,

00:03:34.926 --> 00:03:38.072
he'd already been playing
basketball for 15 goddamn years.

00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:41.220
Even though you all say to
me like, wow, you did it,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.970
I didn't do it, I did it
when I was 14 years old,

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.477
and 15 years old, and 16
years old, and 17 years old,

00:03:46.477 --> 00:03:49.205
and 18 years old, and 19
years old, and 20 years old,

00:03:49.205 --> 00:03:51.427
and 21 years old, 
and 22 years old,

00:03:51.427 --> 00:03:54.064
which are all the years
that every single weekend,

00:03:54.064 --> 00:03:56.504
while my friends 
went to the Jersey shore

00:03:56.504 --> 00:03:58.013
and hooked up with girls,

00:03:58.013 --> 00:03:59.957
while my friends went fishing,

00:03:59.957 --> 00:04:03.026
while my friends hung out
and threw round the football,

00:04:03.026 --> 00:04:05.159
and lived the leisure life,

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:08.144
every weekend, 
every single weekend,

00:04:08.144 --> 00:04:10.593
let me just say it one
more time, every weekend,

00:04:10.593 --> 00:04:12.930
every day, from the
day I got out of school

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.988
to the day I went back into
school, every vacation day,

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.594
all of them, not a good
amount of them, every day,

00:04:18.594 --> 00:04:22.317
from 7am to back
then 8pm, every day,

00:04:22.843 --> 00:04:25.565
I was learning 
the wine business.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:29.069
I was honing my craft
to be a good salesman.

00:04:29.069 --> 00:04:31.595
I was figuring out 
how to be an operator.

00:04:31.595 --> 00:04:34.502
I watched how my dad
interacted with his employees,

00:04:34.502 --> 00:04:36.391
what I liked about it, what I didn't.

00:04:36.391 --> 00:04:38.956
I watched my cousin Bobby
interact with the employees,

00:04:38.956 --> 00:04:41.145
I took what I liked
from it, what I didn't.

00:04:41.145 --> 00:04:44.910
I was 30 years old before
any of you ever saw me.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.266
Go show me the videos
on YouTube right now,

00:04:47.266 --> 00:04:50.038
that have me under 30.
They don't exist.

00:04:50.038 --> 00:04:54.388
I was putting in the work, for
half my life, from 15 to 30,

00:04:54.388 --> 00:04:58.570
where I built an actual
business. I put in actual work,

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.028
and so if you want to tell
me that every goddamn moment

00:05:01.028 --> 00:05:05.074
of my life between 15 and
30 is an overnight success,

00:05:05.074 --> 00:05:08.613
then knock yourself out, but
that is complete bullshit,

00:05:08.613 --> 00:05:09.736
and every one of you know it.

00:05:09.736 --> 00:05:13.621
And so when you email me, 
that you've started this thing,

00:05:13.621 --> 00:05:15.710
that you have the audacity

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.885
to want it to be 
the rest of your life.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:23.212
The audacity, really, 
the entitlement,

00:05:23.212 --> 00:05:24.932
that you think that you
should be able to do something

00:05:24.932 --> 00:05:28.975
that you love so much,
for the rest of your life,

00:05:28.975 --> 00:05:30.738
that makes you enough money,

00:05:30.738 --> 00:05:33.121
to be able to do it for
the rest of your life,

00:05:33.121 --> 00:05:36.546
that you're giving up 
after four months?

00:05:36.546 --> 00:05:38.656
That you're giving up 
after two years?

00:05:38.656 --> 00:05:41.676
As a matter of fact, every
single person watching this video

00:05:41.676 --> 00:05:43.770
should be trying for that moment

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.687
for the rest of 
their life, period.

00:05:48.228 --> 00:05:50.149
You might hit 
pay dirt at 80, and cool,

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:54.310
then you can really do exactly
what you love from 80 to 100.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.432
My friends, it is a gift, 
is a gift,

00:05:57.432 --> 00:06:00.449
to wake up in the morning, and
be able to do what you want,

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:02.616
for the rest of your life.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.009
The way you do that,

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:10.224
is by becoming a quote
unquote, "overnight success".

00:06:10.224 --> 00:06:13.063
You know, the excuse 
that everybody uses

00:06:13.063 --> 00:06:15.371
to deploy against somebody
who's actually put in work,

00:06:15.371 --> 00:06:18.679
for the last decade, and got
themselves into a position

00:06:18.679 --> 00:06:20.139
where they can do 
something pretty rad,

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:22.585
that we all think is cool,
and we all wish we could do.

00:06:22.585 --> 00:06:23.745
You know, that thing,

00:06:23.745 --> 00:06:25.078
the thing that you say to yourself

00:06:25.078 --> 00:06:26.498
to make yourself feel better,

00:06:26.498 --> 00:06:27.585
about when you're laying in bed

00:06:27.585 --> 00:06:29.775
and playing a goddamn 
game on your phone,

00:06:29.775 --> 00:06:32.438
instead of putting in the
work to achieve what you want.

00:06:32.438 --> 00:06:36.605
Nothing in life is free,
nothing happens overnight,

00:06:37.466 --> 00:06:40.005
it all takes tons 
and tons of work,

00:06:40.005 --> 00:06:41.874
and tons and tons of talent,

00:06:41.874 --> 00:06:43.881
and tons and tons of serendipity,

00:06:43.881 --> 00:06:45.721
but my friends, luck, serendipity,

00:06:45.721 --> 00:06:48.542
there's a forced culture within that.

00:06:48.542 --> 00:06:50.525
You know, you'll just sit in your room,

00:06:50.525 --> 00:06:52.514
hoping and then 
something lucky happens,

00:06:52.514 --> 00:06:55.274
nobody just knocks on
your house's door and says

00:06:55.274 --> 00:06:57.530
"Congratulations, you've
been awarded this".

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:00.863
Luck comes from 
being in the right spot.

00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:05.683
I've been really lucky,
because I fucking bleed

00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:08.960
out of my eyes every day of
my life and work my face off.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:14.152
You're really lucky when
you're at that 11:30pm meeting,

00:07:14.152 --> 00:07:16.285
where the lucky thing
happens, pretty cool,

00:07:16.285 --> 00:07:17.964
since all you 
were fucking sleeping.

00:07:17.964 --> 00:07:20.686
I was pretty lucky, weird,
that I scheduled that meeting

00:07:20.686 --> 00:07:22.378
'cause I did a ton of 
things for 30 years,

00:07:22.378 --> 00:07:23.472
that allowed me to 
even have that meeting

00:07:23.472 --> 00:07:25.190
in the first place, that
gave me the leverage

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.707
to have that lucky 
thing that happened.

00:07:28.707 --> 00:07:31.178
There's no overnight successes,
period, they don't exist.

00:07:31.178 --> 00:07:33.275
Show me, 
leave a comment in YouTube,

00:07:33.275 --> 00:07:36.771
leave the name, explain
to me, tell me, show me,

00:07:36.771 --> 00:07:40.591
let me know, show me
the overnight success,

00:07:40.591 --> 00:07:43.908
because I'll show you you,
justifying in your brain,

00:07:43.908 --> 00:07:47.241
something that is 
just not true, period.

00:07:48.203 --> 00:07:52.370
("Inertia" by Irregular Expression)

